Command lists keep fewer entries in place

From upstream EglantinePS5 patch 0024, without its queue size: our GPU command
queue is unbounded (0028). A queue entry is as big as the largest command, and
512 entries in each vector made that about 6.3 KiB, for maps and ticks too.

Adapted from viejunerd/Eglantine-PS5- v1.219.011: its gpu_thread.h hunk (SPSCQueue
0x10000) is left out and the comment is reworded for an unbounded queue. The code
change in dma_pusher.h is the same.

diff --git a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.h b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.h
--- a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.h
+++ b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.h
@@ -113,10 +113,12 @@ struct CommandList final {
     CommandList() = default;
     explicit CommandList(std::size_t size) : command_lists(size) {}
     explicit CommandList(boost::container::small_vector<CommandHeader, 512>&& prefetch_command_list_)
-        : prefetch_command_list{std::move(prefetch_command_list_)} {}
+        : prefetch_command_list(prefetch_command_list_.begin(), prefetch_command_list_.end()) {}
 
-    boost::container::small_vector<CommandListHeader, 512> command_lists;
-    boost::container::small_vector<CommandHeader, 512> prefetch_command_list;
+    // Few entries in place: this struct sits in every slot of the GPU thread's queue, whatever
+    // command the slot holds, and the queue has no limit. Longer lists go on the heap.
+    boost::container::small_vector<CommandListHeader, 32> command_lists;
+    boost::container::small_vector<CommandHeader, 32> prefetch_command_list;
     /// EDEN_NX2_PB_CHECK: hash of each entry's words when it was submitted.
     std::vector<u64> submit_hashes;
     /// The entries' words when they were submitted (NX2), each entry's at submitted_offsets[i]:
